  "label": "Xenophobia",
  "description": "The meme implicitly references xenophobia, which is the fear or dislike of people from other countries or cultures. The phrase 'build a wall to keep yall out' is a direct reference to xenophobic attitudes, suggesting that the wall is meant to exclude people who are perceived as 'foreign' or 'different'. This is a common theme in political rhetoric and can be used to justify exclusionary policies.",
